# 🔴 Mandatory startup protocol

Before writing any code, read these in full, in order:
1. `docs/overview.md` — the spec (line 1 to last line, no skipping by heading)
2. `docs/progress.md` — find your Part. If unassigned, ask the human.
3. `docs/remember.md` — conventions and guardrails (both halves)

Cadence is a Python 3.11 Discord music bot (discord.py 2.x + yt-dlp + FFmpeg).
State is in-memory; there is no database (`overview.md §6`). The whole surface is
nine slash commands (`overview.md §4`). Build order is **A → T1 → (B ∥ C ∥ D) → E →
(T2 ∥ T3)**; parts code against the Protocols in `cadence/interfaces.py`.

# 🔄 Per-turn workflow

Run this every task. No exceptions.

## 1. Plan (in your reply, before any code)
- Task ID you're working on (e.g., `C2-04`)
- Files you'll create or modify (stay inside your Part's owned files — see the Part's
  agent instructions in `progress.md`)
- Which test goes RED first
- Open questions for the human

If anything in your plan contradicts the spec, guardrails, or remember file —
STOP and surface it. Do not silently override.

## 2. Implement (Red-Green-Refactor)
1. Write the test. Run it. Confirm RED.
2. Write the minimum implementation. Run the test. Confirm GREEN.
3. Refactor without breaking the test.

Mock external services — never hit the network, real Discord, or real FFmpeg in
tests (`overview.md §14.5`). Use the fakes from `tests/fakes.py`.

## 3. Document before finishing
- Mark your task `[x]` in `docs/progress.md`
- New gotcha or constraint discovered? Add it to `docs/remember.md` under the right
  section, using the next `G-###` number for guardrails (hard `G-0xx`, style
  `G-1xx`, discovered `G-2xx`).
- Problem that took >1 try? Log it under `remember.md §6` as problem → solution.
- Found a bug in another Part? Don't fix it silently — note it in the Blockers log
  or `remember.md §6` and flag it.

## General rules
- **Never hardcode secrets. Never commit `.env*` files.** (G-001, G-002)
- **Never block the event loop.** Offload yt-dlp / network via
  `loop.run_in_executor`. Re-enter the loop from the FFmpeg `after` thread only via
  `asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe(coro, client.loop)`. (G-003, G-004)
- **Re-resolve stream URLs every play** — they expire; queue stores `webpage_url`,
  not `stream_url`. (G-006)
- `mypy --strict` must pass; **no `Any`**. Type-hint everything. (G-103)
- Depend on the **Protocols** in `cadence/interfaces.py` (`AudioSource`, `Player`),
  not concrete classes. Commands never import `yt_dlp`; sources never import Discord
  interaction types. (G-102)
- User-facing messages follow the emoji + short phrase + **bold track** pattern
  (`overview.md §15`); user errors are ephemeral, internal errors are logged not
  shown. (G-101, G-104)
- Run `ruff check . && mypy cadence && pytest` before marking a task done.
- **Push back is welcome.** If a task seems wrong, contradicts the spec, or has a
  better approach, raise it before implementing.
